# Cursor Rules for CodingCat.dev (.cursorrules)

Always read and follow `AGENTS.md`, `GEMINI.md`, and `DESIGN.md` at the root of this repository before generating code, copy, or visual prompts.

## Critical Rules Summary
1. NEVER use em-dashes anywhere in prose, UI copy, titles, comments, or documentation. Use commas, parentheses, colons, or separate sentences.
2. ALWAYS use Markdown tables for comparisons between tools, frameworks, architectures, or trade-offs.
3. Follow the 13-module CodingCat.dev Design System in `skills/codingcat-design-system/`, `skills/alex-voice-and-copy/`, and `skills/codingcat-media-studio/`:
   - Colors: Canvas Obsidian `#0F172A`, Pure Void `#000000`, Surface Slate `#1E293B`, Elevated `#334155`, Royal Purple `#4B2E83`, Soft Lavender `#B4A7D6`, Electric Lime `#C5E86C`, Mint `#86EFAC`, Coral `#FCA5A5`, Text Primary `#F8FAFC`, Text Muted `#94A3B8`.
   - Typography: `Nunito` (800/900) for chunky H1 display titles, `Inter` for UI and H2-H6, `JetBrains Mono` for code/badges, and `Virgil` / `Excalifont` for dark-mode Excalidraw diagram explanations.
   - Mascot Assets: Use canonical files in `assets/` (`AJHeadphones.png`, `AJ-2D-Bipedal.jpg`, `AJ-3D-Headphones-Front.jpg`, `AJ-3D-Headphones-Left.jpg`, `AJ-3D-Headphones-Right.jpg`).
